<article class="env-example" id="0DJC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DJC">Example <span data-tag="0DJC">53.10.6</span>.</a> In fact, the situation described in Lemma <a href="/tag/0DJB" data-tag="0DJB">53.10.5</a> occurs for any nontrivial finite extension $k'/k$. Namely, we can consider </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  A = \{ f \in k'[x] \mid f(0) \in k \}   \]
</div>
  <p> The spectrum of $A$ is an affine curve, which we can glue to the spectrum of $B = k'[y]$ using the isomorphism $A_ x \cong B_ y$ sending $x^{-1}$ to $y$. The result is a proper curve $X$ with $H^0(X, \mathcal{O}_ X) = k$ and singular point $x$ corresponding to the maximal ideal $A \cap (x)$. The normalization of $X$ is $\mathbf{P}^1_{k'}$ exactly as in the lemma. </p>
</article>